# NEXIS SITTA - Vibecoding Guidelines

## Tech Stack
- Framework: Next.js 16 (App Router) with TypeScript
- Database & Auth: Supabase (PostgreSQL with RLS)
- Styling: Tailwind CSS v4 (utility classes; Shadcn/ui is NOT installed yet)

## Code Style & Rules
1. Always write clean, production-ready TypeScript code without using `any`.
2. All database queries must respect Supabase Row Level Security (RLS).
   Never accept `organization_id` from user input — bind it from
   `getSessionContext()` in `src/lib/auth/session.ts`.
3. Separate Server Components and Client Components appropriately ('use client' only when needed).
   Prefer Server Components for data fetching; use Server Actions for mutations.
4. Use modern async/await patterns for Next.js App Router server actions.
5. A `'use server'` module may only export async functions. Shared state
   objects and interfaces belong in a separate non-server module
   (see `src/lib/auth/types.ts`, `src/lib/products/types.ts`).